questions.scenario:
You are debugging a production issue where high-throughput concurrent updates to a custom `ConcurrentHashMap<TransactionKey, TransactionData>` cache result in memory leaks and unexpected cache misses. Lookups fail even when keys are demonstrably present in the map keyset.

Bug Hunter Snippet:
java
public class TransactionKey {
    private final String transactionId;
    private final List<String> metadataTags;

    public TransactionKey(String transactionId, List<String> metadataTags) {
        this.transactionId = transactionId;
        this.metadataTags = metadataTags;
    }

    public void addTag(String tag) {
        this.metadataTags.add(tag);
    }

    @Override
    public boolean equals(Object o) {
        if (this == o) return true;
        if (!(o instanceof TransactionKey)) return false;
        TransactionKey that = (TransactionKey) o;
        return Objects.equals(transactionId, that.transactionId) &&
               Objects.equals(metadataTags, that.metadataTags);
    }

    @Override
    public int hashCode() {
        return Objects.hash(transactionId, metadataTags);
    }
}
